1	//! Git sidecar branch storage — metadata on orphan branch, code on working branch.
2	//!
3	//! All writes to the sidecar branch(es) go through git plumbing (hash-object,
4	//! update-index against a scratch index, write-tree, commit-tree, update-ref) rather
5	//! than `git checkout`. This is deliberate: an earlier checkout-based design forced the
6	//! *primary* working tree onto the sidecar branch to build a commit there, and any
7	//! failure partway through left the repo stranded mid-operation with uncommitted work
8	//! discarded. Plumbing never touches the working tree or HEAD, so that failure mode is
9	//! structurally impossible — worst case, nothing happens and the error surfaces cleanly.
10	
11	use anyhow::{bail, Context, Result};
12	use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
13	use std::process::Command;
14	use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicU64, Ordering};
